# stream-join — AI Agent Rules

## Project identity

`stream-join` joins values from multiple object-mode Readable streams into a single object-mode Readable with proper backpressure. The npm package name is `stream-join`. It is built on top of `stream-chain` (`readableFrom`) and is part of the `stream-chain` / `stream-json` family.

## Critical rules

- **CommonJS.** The project is `"type": "commonjs"`. Use `require()` in source, `import` in tests (`.mjs`).
- **No transpilation.** Code runs directly.
- **One runtime dependency: `stream-chain`.** Never add other packages to `dependencies`.
- **Built on `stream-chain`.** Use `stream-chain/utils/readableFrom` as the foundation; do not hand-roll `Readable` + pause/resume.
- **Object mode is always on.** The output Readable forces `objectMode: true`.
- **Backpressure must be handled correctly** — async iteration via `readableFrom` is the mechanism.
- **Do not modify or delete test expectations** without understanding why they changed.
- **Do not add comments or remove comments** unless explicitly asked.
- **Keep `src/index.js` and `src/index.d.ts` in sync.**

## Code style

- Prettier: 100 char width, single quotes, no bracket spacing, no trailing commas, arrow parens "avoid" (see `.prettierrc`).
- 2-space indentation.
- Semicolons are enforced by Prettier (default `semi: true`).

## Architecture quick reference

- `join(streams, options)` is the only public export.
- Input streams: object-mode Node `Readable`. Consumed via `[Symbol.asyncIterator]()`.
- Per-round: `Promise.all(iters.map(it => it.next()))` pulls one value from each non-ended stream concurrently; ended streams contribute `null`.
- Errors: a side-listener captures the original `'error'` value before Node's async-iterator destroys the stream with an `AbortError` wrapper; the captured error is re-thrown.
- `joinItems(sink, items)` combines per-round values. Default: `(sink, items) => sink.push(items)`.
- The output is `readableFrom({iterable: zip, objectMode: true, ...})` from `stream-chain`.

## Verification commands

- `npm test` — run the full test suite (parallel workers)
- `node tests/test-<name>.mjs` — run a single test file directly
- `npm run test:bun` — run with Bun
- `npm run test:deno` — run with Deno
- `npm run ts-check` — TypeScript type checking
- `npm run js-check` — `tsc --allowJs --checkJs` over the JS sources
- `npm run lint` — Prettier check
- `npm run lint:fix` — Prettier write

## File layout

- Entry point: `src/index.js` + `src/index.d.ts`
- Tests: `tests/test-*.mjs`, `tests/test-*.cjs`, `tests/helpers.mjs`
- Wiki docs: `wiki/` (git submodule)

## When reading the codebase

- Start with `ARCHITECTURE.md` for the module map.
- `src/index.d.ts` is the canonical API reference.
- The `tests/` files demonstrate every supported usage pattern.
- Wiki markdown files in `wiki/` contain detailed usage docs.
